===Suffix===
{{head|de|suffixes|cat2=noun-forming suffixes|plural|-lein|or|-leins|or|-erlein|cat3=diminutive suffixes}}

# {{non-gloss definition|suffix used to create a [[diminutive]] form; e.g. ''Kind'' → ''Kind'''lein'''''}}

====Usage notes====
* In contemporary Standard German {{m|de||-lein}} is usual with words whose stems end in ''-ch'' and, to a lesser degree, in ''-g''; thus more often {{m|de|Bächlein|t=little brook}} than {{m|de|Bächelchen}}. There is also a limited number of other forms that remain in common use, but in most cases {{m|de||-lein}} now has a poetic and archaic tone. The general diminutive suffix in the written language and in northern speech is {{m|de|-chen}}, while southern informal use prefers regional suffixes like {{m|de|-le}}, {{m|de|-li}} (Swabian/Alemannic) and {{m|de|-erl}} (Austro-Bavarian).
* The plural generally remains unchanged as it does with diminutives in {{m|de||-chen}}. A few nouns with a plural in {{m|de|-er}} may carry the same ending over to the plural diminutive. This is common with {{m|de|Kindlein}} → {{m|de||Kinderlein}} (and equally {{m|de|Kindchen}} → {{m|de||Kinderchen}}); otherwise it is rare. A few nouns referring to people allow a plural in ''-s''. This is common with {{m|de|Fräulein}} → {{m|de||Fräuleins}}; otherwise it is, again, rare.

